.idea/

# Generated by `flutter create`. android/ and ios/ ARE committed (see
# README.md) because real customizations live there (permissions, launcher
# icons, release signing config) that flutter_launcher_icons/flutter create
# don't reproduce — losing that folder means losing those features on the
# next build even though the code is on GitHub. Their own nested
# android/.gitignore and ios/.gitignore already exclude the machine-specific
# bits (local.properties, .gradle/, Pods/, ephemeral/, keystores).
# macos/windows/linux/web are unused desktop/web scaffolding with no
# customization, so they stay generated-only.
macos/
windows/
linux/
web/
